`/app/fixture/package.json` — both blocks updated (only file touched, left uncommitted):

```diff
   "peerDependencies": {
-    "@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent": "^0.1.0-rc.8"
+    "@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent": "^0.1.2-alpha.2"
   },
   "devDependencies": {
-    "@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent": "^0.1.0-rc.8"
+    "@deepseek-ai/dsh-agent": "^0.1.2-alpha.2"
   },
```

## Why this bound

npm's prerelease rule only lets a prerelease version satisfy a range when a comparator in the range carries a prerelease on the **same** `major.minor.patch` tuple. `^0.1.0-rc.8` carries its prerelease on `0.1.0`, so `0.1.2-alpha.2` (and `0.1.2-rc.1`) could never match. Moving the lower bound into the 0.1.2 tuple, `^0.1.2-alpha.2`:

- matches `0.1.2-alpha.2` and the rest of the 0.1.2 prerelease/stabilization cohort,
- still rejects the legacy `0.1.0-rc.8`, `0.1.1`, `0.1.3-alpha.1`, and `0.2.0` (verified with semver; `minVersion` is exactly `0.1.2-alpha.2`),
- stays bounded (`<0.2.0`), unlike `*` — which, notably, also wouldn't match the prerelease target at all.

